@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: FLS Routing
	Testing the routing of specific tickets from FLS organizations to FLS user groups

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown users with the following userExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| User1 |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Organization1 |

Scenario: FLS CN Routing
	End users who create requests for a China support organization with partner first line support for specific products and components should have their requests routed to the FLS - CN group.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status                     | Approved            |
	| Name                       | Organization Name 1 |
	| Shared Tickets             | true                |
	| Shared Comments            | true                |
	| SLA                        | Gold                |
	| Tier                       | Regular             |
	| Support Region             | China               |
	| Support Language           | Chinese             |
	| Partner First Line Support | true                | 
	| External ID                | Organization1       |
	And I assign an organization with organizationExternalId "Organization1" with the following tags
	| developer_tools            |
	| enterprise_search_premium  |
	| enterprise_search_standard |
	| liferay_commerce           |
	| liferay_dxp                |
	| liferay_portal             |
	| management_tools_lcs       |
	| mobile_device_detection    |
	| mobile_experience          |
	| productivity_tools_sync    |
	| social_office              |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Chinese                          |
	| Time Zone        | Beijing                          | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product and component values
	| prd_developer_tools            |                                        |
	| prd_enterprise_search_premium  | monitoring                             |
	| prd_enterprise_search_standard | elasticsearch                          |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_1_1       | apis_integrations_and_extension_points |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_2_0       | commerce_insights                      |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_2            | apio_architect                         |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_1            | application_display_templates          |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_0            | audience_targeting                     |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2         | authentication                         |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_1         | caching_clustering                     |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_0         | calendar                               |
	| prd_liferay_portal_5_2         | collaboration_suite                    |
	| prd_management_tools_lcs       |                                        |
	| prd_mobile_device_detection    |                                        |
	| prd_mobile_experience          |                                        |
	| prd_productivity_tools_sync    |                                        |
	| prd_social_office              |                                        |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be assigned to the group "FLS - CN"

