Scenario: CSE CN Routing for FLS Organizations
	End users who create requests for a China support organization with partner first line support for specific products and components should have their requests routed to the CSE - CN group.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status                     | Approved            |
	| Name                       | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags                       | liferay_portal      |
	| Shared Tickets             | true                |
	| Shared Comments            | true                |
	| SLA                        | Gold                |
	| Tier                       | Regular             |
	| Support Region             | China               |
	| Support Language           | Chinese             |
	| Partner First Line Support | true                |
	| External ID                | Organization1       |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Chinese                          |
	| Time Zone        | Beijing                          | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product and component values
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2 | patch_management |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be assigned to the group "CSE - CN"

